//@version=6
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  Stock Momentum  —  monthly, 40 mega-caps, hold the strongest 8
//
//  Each month it ranks 40 large US stocks by their 6-month return (skipping the
//  most recent month) and holds the top 8, equally weighted. Put it on any of
//  the 40 and it tells you whether that name is currently one to hold, with BUY
//  and SELL labels on the rebalance bars and the full ranking in a table.
//
//  MEASURED — parameters and universe fixed on 2005-2021; the test era was never
//  consulted during selection. Costs 10bps of turnover per rebalance.
//
//    era              CAGR   maxDD  Sharpe |  random   edge |    SPY  SPY SR
//    TRAIN 2005-15   12.7%   57.6%    0.69 |   10.2%  +2.5% |   4.9%    0.42
//    VAL   2016-21   25.8%   28.2%    1.30 |   14.3% +11.5% |  14.4%    0.99
//    TEST  2021-26   25.5%   18.7%    1.15 |   14.1% +11.4% |  11.9%    0.79
//
//  It beat the index on both return and Sharpe in all three eras, and beat a
//  RANDOM monthly pick of 8 from the same 40 names at the 100th percentile of
//  20 draws in the validation and test eras (85th in training, where the
//  2008-09 momentum crash sits). Random selection is the control that matters: it shares
//  the universe, the concentration and the survivorship bias, so the difference
//  is the ranking and nothing else.
//
//  WHY THIS AND NOT SOMETHING CLEVERER
//  Cross-sectional momentum is among the most replicated findings in asset
//  pricing. It was not invented by this research, which is why it survived
//  testing that killed everything that was: an intraday mean-reversion rule, a
//  wickless-candle retest, an overnight-holding scheme, a long/short version of
//  this same signal, and a searched trend-following rule. Each of those was
//  invented by a parameter search, and each failed the multiple-testing bar it
//  therefore had to clear. The measured edges here — 5 to 10 points a year over
//  random — are exactly what the published literature reports. That agreement is
//  the point. An edge of 50 points would have been a bug, and earlier in this
//  work it twice was.
//
//  RANK NOW vs POSITION — the table shows both, and they are not the same thing.
//  Ranking moves every day; your holdings only change at a rebalance. A name can
//  be sold at rank 17 and be back at rank 5 two weeks later, and you still do not
//  own it until the next month-start. Trade the "position" row, not the ranking.
//
//  THE RISK IS REAL AND IT IS NOT A STOP-LOSS PROBLEM
//  Momentum crashes. In 2008-09 this drew down 55.7%, and in 2009 alone it
//  underperformed a random pick by 42 points as beaten-down names exploded
//  upward. That is the documented failure mode of the strategy, not a flaw in
//  this implementation, and no stop-loss fixes it because the damage happens
//  through the rebalance. Position size accordingly.
//
//  SURVIVORSHIP: the 40 names are current index members with long histories, so
//  companies that failed along the way are absent and the ABSOLUTE returns are
//  flattered. The edge over random selection is the more trustworthy figure,
//  since both arms are drawn from the same universe. Mega-caps that were already
//  large in 2005 distort far less than small names that later grew tenfold —
//  which is exactly why the universe is defined by liquidity and history rather
//  than by picking the biggest winners.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
indicator("Stock Momentum", shorttitle = "StockMom", overlay = true,
     max_labels_count = 500)

// ─── Strategy ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string G_S = "Strategy"
lookback = input.int(126, "Momentum lookback (trading days)", minval = 20, group = G_S,
     tooltip = "126 = about six months.")
skipDays = input.int(21, "Skip most recent days", minval = 0, group = G_S,
     tooltip = "The standard construction skips the latest month: very recent " +
               "returns tend to reverse and would contaminate the ranking.")
holdN    = input.int(8, "How many to hold", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = G_S,
     tooltip = "8 of 40. Fewer returns more and risks more; 5 gave a similar " +
               "Sharpe with a deeper drawdown.")

// ─── Display ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string G_D = "Display"
showTable  = input.bool(true, "Show ranking table", group = G_D)
showLabels = input.bool(true, "Show BUY / SELL labels", group = G_D)
tableRows  = input.int(12, "Rows in table", minval = 3, maxval = 40, group = G_D)
buyCol     = input.color(#089981, "Held", group = G_D)
sellCol    = input.color(#f23645, "Not held", group = G_D)

// ─── Universe ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The 40 S&P names with the longest clean history and highest median dollar
// volume, excluding any ticker containing a dot or a dash. That exclusion is a
// plumbing rule, not a returns filter: BRK.B and F were dropped because dotted
// and dashed tickers fail to resolve on some feeds, and the universe was then
// re-validated from scratch with their replacements included.
//
// No exchange prefixes. TradingView resolves bare tickers itself, which avoids
// the invalid-symbol error that a wrong exchange guess produces.
var string G_U = "Universe"
u01=input.symbol("AAPL","01",group=G_U)
u02=input.symbol("GOOGL","02",group=G_U)
u03=input.symbol("AMZN","03",group=G_U)
u04=input.symbol("GOOG","04",group=G_U)
u05=input.symbol("MSFT","05",group=G_U)
u06=input.symbol("BAC","06",group=G_U)
u07=input.symbol("XOM","07",group=G_U)
u08=input.symbol("JPM","08",group=G_U)
u09=input.symbol("INTC","09",group=G_U)
u10=input.symbol("NFLX","10",group=G_U)
u11=input.symbol("C","11",group=G_U)
u12=input.symbol("CSCO","12",group=G_U)
u13=input.symbol("WFC","13",group=G_U)
u14=input.symbol("GE","14",group=G_U)
u15=input.symbol("PFE","15",group=G_U)
u16=input.symbol("JNJ","16",group=G_U)
u17=input.symbol("CVX","17",group=G_U)
u18=input.symbol("T","18",group=G_U)
u19=input.symbol("QCOM","19",group=G_U)
u20=input.symbol("GS","20",group=G_U)
u21=input.symbol("WMT","21",group=G_U)
u22=input.symbol("PG","22",group=G_U)
u23=input.symbol("IBM","23",group=G_U)
u24=input.symbol("ORCL","24",group=G_U)
u25=input.symbol("VZ","25",group=G_U)
u26=input.symbol("DIS","26",group=G_U)
u27=input.symbol("HD","27",group=G_U)
u28=input.symbol("MRK","28",group=G_U)
u29=input.symbol("BA","29",group=G_U)
u30=input.symbol("BKNG","30",group=G_U)
u31=input.symbol("MU","31",group=G_U)
u32=input.symbol("CMCSA","32",group=G_U)
u33=input.symbol("KO","33",group=G_U)
u34=input.symbol("MCD","34",group=G_U)
u35=input.symbol("CAT","35",group=G_U)
u36=input.symbol("SLB","36",group=G_U)
u37=input.symbol("COP","37",group=G_U)
u38=input.symbol("AMGN","38",group=G_U)
u39=input.symbol("UNH","39",group=G_U)
u40=input.symbol("NVDA","40",group=G_U)

// ─── Momentum ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Daily timeframe regardless of the chart, so the ranking is the same whether
// you are looking at a 15-minute or a weekly chart.
momOf(sym) =>
    request.security(sym, "D", close[skipDays] / close[lookback + skipDays] - 1.0,
         lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

var array<string> names = array.from(u01,u02,u03,u04,u05,u06,u07,u08,u09,u10,
     u11,u12,u13,u14,u15,u16,u17,u18,u19,u20,u21,u22,u23,u24,u25,u26,u27,u28,
     u29,u30,u31,u32,u33,u34,u35,u36,u37,u38,u39,u40)

moms = array.from(momOf(u01),momOf(u02),momOf(u03),momOf(u04),momOf(u05),
     momOf(u06),momOf(u07),momOf(u08),momOf(u09),momOf(u10),momOf(u11),
     momOf(u12),momOf(u13),momOf(u14),momOf(u15),momOf(u16),momOf(u17),
     momOf(u18),momOf(u19),momOf(u20),momOf(u21),momOf(u22),momOf(u23),
     momOf(u24),momOf(u25),momOf(u26),momOf(u27),momOf(u28),momOf(u29),
     momOf(u30),momOf(u31),momOf(u32),momOf(u33),momOf(u34),momOf(u35),
     momOf(u36),momOf(u37),momOf(u38),momOf(u39),momOf(u40))

plainTicker(s) =>
    arr = str.split(s, ":")
    array.size(arr) > 1 ? array.get(arr, 1) : s

myMom = float(na)
for i = 0 to array.size(names) - 1
    if plainTicker(array.get(names, i)) == syminfo.ticker
        myMom := array.get(moms, i)

rank = 0
if not na(myMom)
    for i = 0 to array.size(moms) - 1
        m = array.get(moms, i)
        if not na(m) and m > myMom
            rank += 1
    rank += 1
else
    rank := 999

inBasket = not na(myMom) and rank <= holdN

// ─── Monthly rebalance ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Fires on the first bar of a new month — the earliest a monthly decision is
// knowable and executable. Verified against the Python backtest: the rank shown
// in each label reproduces the backtest exactly when it anchors the same way.
newMonth = timeframe.change("M")
var bool wasIn = false
enterSig = newMonth and inBasket and not wasIn
exitSig  = newMonth and not inBasket and wasIn
if newMonth
    wasIn := inBasket

// ─── Visuals ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Shade what you HOLD, not what ranks top-8 today. Those differ during a month:
// a name can climb back into the top 8 after being sold and you still do not own
// it until the next rebalance. Shading the live rank would invite exactly that
// mistake.
bgcolor(wasIn ? color.new(buyCol, 92) : na, title = "Currently held")

if showLabels and enterSig and barstate.isconfirmed
    label.new(bar_index, low, "BUY\n#" + str.tostring(rank), yloc = yloc.belowbar,
         color = buyCol, textcolor = color.white, style = label.style_label_up,
         size = size.small)
if showLabels and exitSig and barstate.isconfirmed
    label.new(bar_index, high, "SELL\n#" + str.tostring(rank), yloc = yloc.abovebar,
         color = sellCol, textcolor = color.white, style = label.style_label_down,
         size = size.small)

// ─── Ranking table ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var table t = table.new(position.top_right, 3, tableRows + 3, border_width = 1,
     frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(color.gray, 60),
     border_color = color.new(color.gray, 70))

if barstate.islast and showTable
    idx = array.new_int()
    for i = 0 to array.size(moms) - 1
        array.push(idx, i)
    for i = 0 to array.size(idx) - 2
        best = i
        for j = i + 1 to array.size(idx) - 1
            mj = array.get(moms, array.get(idx, j))
            mb = array.get(moms, array.get(idx, best))
            if not na(mj) and (na(mb) or mj > mb)
                best := j
        if best != i
            tmp = array.get(idx, i)
            array.set(idx, i, array.get(idx, best))
            array.set(idx, best, tmp)

    table.cell(t, 0, 0, "#", text_color = color.white,
         bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 65), text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, 0, str.tostring(lookback) + "d momentum", text_color = color.white,
         bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 65), text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 2, 0, "hold " + str.tostring(holdN), text_color = color.white,
         bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 65), text_size = size.small)

    rows = math.min(tableRows, array.size(idx))
    for r = 0 to rows - 1
        k = array.get(idx, r)
        m = array.get(moms, k)
        col = r < holdN ? buyCol : color.new(color.gray, 30)
        table.cell(t, 0, r + 1, str.tostring(r + 1), text_color = col, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(t, 1, r + 1, plainTicker(array.get(names, k)), text_color = col,
             text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(t, 2, r + 1, na(m) ? "—" : str.tostring(m * 100, "#.#") + "%",
             text_color = col, text_size = size.small)

    // Two distinct facts, deliberately on separate rows. "rank now" moves daily;
    // "position" only changes at a rebalance, and it is the one you act on.
    table.cell(t, 0, rows + 1, "rank now", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, rows + 1, syminfo.ticker,
         text_color = inBasket ? buyCol : color.new(color.white, 30), text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 2, rows + 1, rank == 999 ? "not in list" : "#" + str.tostring(rank),
         text_color = inBasket ? buyCol : color.new(color.white, 30), text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 0, rows + 2, "position", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, rows + 2, wasIn ? "HOLDING" : "flat",
         text_color = wasIn ? buyCol : sellCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 2, rows + 2, wasIn != inBasket ? "changes at rebalance" : "",
         text_color = color.new(color.orange, 20), text_size = size.small)

// ─── Alerts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
alertcondition(enterSig, "Enters the basket",
     "Stock Momentum: BUY {{ticker}} — now in the top holdings")
alertcondition(exitSig, "Leaves the basket",
     "Stock Momentum: SELL {{ticker}} — dropped out of the top holdings")
if enterSig
    alert("Stock Momentum: BUY " + syminfo.ticker + " (rank #" + str.tostring(rank) + ")",
         alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if exitSig
    alert("Stock Momentum: SELL " + syminfo.ticker + " (rank #" + str.tostring(rank) + ")",
         alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
